g", "description": "(26 Jul 2007) SHOTLIST\r\n1. Wide exterior of FIA (Federation Internationale de l'Automobile) building in paris \r\n2. FIA flag flying over building \r\n3. Various of FIA officials arriving \r\n4. McLaren Formula One team principal Ron Dennis walking into building - Formula One President Bernie Ecclestone in background \r\n5. Ferrari Team Director Jean Todt walking in   \r\n6. Various of journalists outside entrance to FIA building \r\nSTORYLINE:\r\nFormula One leader McLaren-Mercedes went before a hearing on Thursday to answer charges that its designer acquired confidential information from rival Ferrari.\r\nIf found guilty, the team could have points deducted, be temporarily banned from races, or even be thrown out of the Formula One championship.\r\nThe hearing at FIA's (Federation Internationale de l'Automobile) world motor sport council in Paris will examine how confidential data belonging to Ferrari ended up with suspended McLaren chief designer Mike Coughlan - and if other team officials were aware of the contents.\r\nFIA asked that McLaren answer a charge that it broke the sport's code by acquiring documents and confidential information belonging to Ferrari, \"including information that could be used to design, engineer, build, check, test, develop and/or run a 2007 Ferrari Formula One car.\"\r\nFerrari will be represented at the hearing by team director Jean Todt, while McLaren team principal Ron Dennis will be there for his team.\r\nAccording to a report in the Italian sports newspaper, Gazzetta dello Sport, Todt - who sits on the world motor sport council - will abstain from the vote over any potential punishment.\r\nMcLaren has said that its cars do not contain any Ferrari-related alterations and that the company suspended an employee for receiving a package of technical information from the Italian team. \r\nBritish newspapers identified the employee as Coughlan.\r\nCriminal investigations into the affair are still under way in Italy and Britain.\r\n\r\nFind out more about AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/HowWeWork \r\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/AP_Archive \r\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/APArchives ​​\r\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/APNews/\r\n\r\n\r\nYou can license this story through AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/metadata/youtube/97100756bd4c3852589928391ab69f99", "channel_id": "UCHTK-2W11Vh1V4uwofOfR4w", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCHTK-2W11Vh1V4uwofOfR4w", "duration": 62, "view_count": 255, "age_limit": 0, "webpage_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5VpWXoVse6k", "categories": ["News & Politics"], "tags": ["AP Archive", "530987", "97100756bd4c3852589928391ab69f99", "France Formula 1"], "playable_in_embed": true, "live_status": "not_live", "media_type": "video", "_format_sort_fields": ["quality", "res", "fps", "hdr:12", "source", "vcodec", "channels", "acodec", "lang", "proto"], "automatic_captions": {}, "subtitles": {}, "like_count": 2, "channel": "AP Archive", "channel_follower_count": 6060000, "channel_is_verified": true, "uploader": "AP Archive", "uploader_id": "@APArchive", "uploader_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@APArchive", "upload_date": "20150721", "timestamp": 1437486399, "availability": "public", "webpage_url_basename": "watch", "webpage_url_domain": "youtube.com", "extractor": "youtube", "extractor_key": "Youtube", "display_id": "5VpWXoVse6k", "fulltitle": "Hearing opens on charges McLaren stole information from rival Ferrari", "duration_string": "1:02", "is_live": false, "was_live": false, "epoch": 1794439988, "format": "605 - 640x360+140 - audio only (medium)", "format_id": "605+140", "ext": "mp4", "protocol": "m3u8_native+https", "format_note": "medium", "filesize_approx": 1006365, "tbr": 680.294, "width": 640, "height": 360, "resolution": "640x360", "fps": 25.0, "dynamic_range": "SDR", "vcodec": "vp09.00.21.08", "vbr": 550.725, "aspect_ratio": 1.78, "acodec": "mp4a.40.2", "abr": 129.569, "asr": 44100, "audio_channels": 2, 